ly writer  alone was too i knew that my all my  intuition says the reporter was that  that he would be asked something when he  got to Bergstrom and so I in Washington  yes and not Bergstrom the Andrews Air  Force Base and I block printed out those  58 words that he used this is a sad time  for all people and ending up I asked  your help and gods and I headed it when  Bill Moyers took a helicopter he and I  handed it to him and he showed that the  President and he liked it and he used it  and but I can't take any credit from  those words I mean they were handed to  me and I just  I'm grateful I was there to have that  small role but I guess they're the most  important words I've ever written but  I've written lots of others we did were  you present at the swearing-in yes  pressed against the back wall my you  felt so awful you felt so you want to  shrink from the scene almost that was my  feeling and we were all called into that  cabin and we you know it was you were  jolted I was very conscious that this  had happened in Texas all of us were it  was made things tougher and then I flew  back with them and as we got off the  plane on the welder helicopter on the  steps on the lawn of the White House the  president said go with Lady Bird and  help her all you can well you know I was  on a trip to Japan when President  Kennedy was assassinated I was with six  members of his cabinet going to a an  economic conference in Tokyo and  although I hadn't been sent to  participate in the economic conference I  was sent because President Kennedy  wanted me to organize his visit there in  February of 1964 he would have been the  first united states president to visit  japan since the end of World War two but  we were about two hours out of Honolulu  where we had spent the night when the  word came that he'd been shot and then  the word came that he had been killed  and we got back to the white house at  about two o'clock the next morning it  was a very I mean it was just about t