aught me that while  the world light and the White House may  flicker the light in the White House  never never never goes out the  constitutional bindings that hold this  nation together stronger than any person  or group and the assassination of a  president a war a depression plague  pestilence all of these shatter against  this shield of the Constitution and it's  very comforting to know that even in the  time of the most terrifying and  terrorizing disaster the country goes on

